Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-17-2001||03:23 PM||||How many different sizes of sunroofs came on the 1984 fiero?<P>And what other changes were different from the econo fiero vs the regular 84 sc/se?<P>I noticed my 1984 stock sunroof is a lot smaller then another stock sunroof fiero I was looking at, and my car seems to be about 4 inches longer then this econo coupe is? (we lined them up exactly side by side)<P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Seanh||06-17-2001||03:45 PM||||No kidding hu? I didn't think there were any different sunroof's on Fiero's. Only real differences I know of on a ecno car is lack of everything optional. I also don't think there should be any difference in size either. I don't own an econ coupe, so I can't be for sure, but I'v just never heard anything about these things. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||06-17-2001||03:45 PM||||There was only one kind of sunroof from the factory and it was pretty big. Yours sounds like an aftermarket job from the dealer. <P>Your 84 is 4 inches longer than the other 84? Since all 84s used the same body panels and chassis I don't see how that could happen! Econo vs SC/SE differences were only option packages. No body stretch options there!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodrv6||06-17-2001||03:48 PM||||All factory sunroofs are identical.  If there is a difference in sunroof size, then one of them is an aftermarket installation.  The only differences between an econo 84 coupe and an SE are the final drive ratio and fewer options were available on the econo coupe.  There are also some differences in the suspension---spring rates, wheel size, and possibly steering ratio.  All Fiero's had the same wheel base and the same chassis dimensions.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
